repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/dissipative-computation"
abstract: >-
  Simulation code, banked convergence-audited data records, and figure-generation
  scripts for a study of Landauer-gated cellular automata competing over a shared
  diffusing energy field. Each state-changing transition is charged against a
  local energy budget. A single structural property of each rule -- whether it
  admits an absorbing configuration -- organizes both single-rule energetic
  demand and multi-rule competitive outcomes.
keywords:
  - cellular automata
  - non-equilibrium thermodynamics
  - Landauer principle
  - spatial ecology
  - absorbing states
